+# Secrets referenced from config/deploy.yml. This file is committed, so it must
+# not contain raw credentials. Fill them in by exporting the variables before
+# `kamal setup`, or replace the right-hand side with a command that prints the
+# secret (a password manager, `cat` of a gitignored file, etc.).
+#
+# Generate SECRET_KEY_BASE once and keep it. A new value on every deploy logs
+# everyone out:
+#
+#   bin/rails secret
+#
+# SMTP_USERNAME / SMTP_PASSWORD are whatever your mail server requires. If it
+# does not use authentication, leave these empty and remove them from
+# env.secret in config/deploy.yml.
+
+SECRET_KEY_BASE=$SECRET_KEY_BASE
+SMTP_USERNAME=$SMTP_USERNAME
+SMTP_PASSWORD=$SMTP_PASSWORD
+
+# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
+# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=$VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=$VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
