   config.action_mailer.perform_caching = false
 
-  # Ignore bad email addresses and do not raise email delivery errors.
-  # Set this to true and configure the email server for immediate delivery to raise delivery errors.
-  # config.action_mailer.raise_delivery_errors = false
+  # One-box deploys set APP_HOST to the kamal-proxy hostname so mail, notifications,
+  # and webhooks link to https://that-host rather than an internal container name.
+  host = ENV["APP_HOST"].presence
+  if host
+    url_options = { host: host, protocol: "https" }
+    config.action_mailer.default_url_options = url_options
+    config.action_controller.default_url_options = url_options
+    config.after_initialize do
+      Rails.application.routes.default_url_options = url_options
+    end
+  end
+
+  # Outbound mail. config/deploy.yml sets SMTP_ADDRESS to the forker's mail server.
+  # Credentials come from .kamal/secrets. Servers without auth can omit them.
+  if ENV["SMTP_ADDRESS"].present?
+    config.action_mailer.delivery_method = :smtp
+    config.action_mailer.raise_delivery_errors = true
+
+    smtp_settings = {
+      address: ENV["SMTP_ADDRESS"],
+      port: Integer(ENV.fetch("SMTP_PORT", 587)),
+      domain: ENV["SMTP_DOMAIN"].presence,
+      enable_starttls_auto: ENV.fetch("SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO", "true") == "true"
+    }
+
+    if ENV["SMTP_SSL"] == "true"
+      smtp_settings[:ssl] = true
+      smtp_settings[:enable_starttls_auto] = false
+    end
+
+    if ENV["SMTP_USERNAME"].present?
+      smtp_settings[:user_name] = ENV["SMTP_USERNAME"]
+      smtp_settings[:password] = ENV["SMTP_PASSWORD"]
+      smtp_settings[:authentication] = ENV.fetch("SMTP_AUTHENTICATION", "plain").to_sym
+    end
+
+    config.action_mailer.smtp_settings = smtp_settings.compact
+  end
 
   # Enable locale fallbacks for I18n (makes lookups for any locale fall back to
   # the I18n.default_locale when a translation cannot be found).
diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..596cdc3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+## Deploying on one box
+
+Fizzy ships a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) config for a single Linux server: Docker, SQLite, the web process and background jobs in one container, TLS from kamal-proxy. Someone who forks the repo fills in a hostname, a mail server, and secrets, then runs `kamal setup`.
+
+The app will be at `https://<host>`. SQLite databases and uploaded files live on the `fizzy_storage` volume mounted at `/rails/storage`, so they survive the next `kamal deploy`.
+
+### What you need
+
+- A Linux server you can SSH to. `kamal setup` installs Docker if it is missing.
+- A DNS name pointing at that server. Ports 80 and 443 must be reachable for Let's Encrypt.
+- An SMTP server. Login is a magic link, so Fizzy cannot be used without outbound mail.
+- Kamal installed locally (`gem install kamal`) or via `bin/kamal` from this repo. Run commands from the repository root. Do not enable SaaS mode; `bin/kamal` then reads `config/deploy.yml`.
+
+### Fill in
+
+1. `config/deploy.yml` — the two anchors at the top:
+   - `x-host` — public hostname (also the SSH target, unless you split that line).
+   - `x-mail-server` — SMTP hostname. Adjust `x-mail-from` so it is an address that server will send.
+2. `.kamal/secrets` — `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `SMTP_USERNAME`, and `SMTP_PASSWORD`. Export them, or point each assignment at a command. Generate the key once with `bin/rails secret` and keep it. Do not commit raw secrets.
+
+The registry defaults to Kamal's local registry, so you do not need Docker Hub. See the comments in `config/deploy.yml` to push to GHCR or Docker Hub instead, or to build `arm64`.
+
+### Setup
+
+```sh
+kamal setup
+```
+
+That bootstraps Docker, obtains a certificate for the hostname, builds the image, and boots Fizzy. Background jobs run in the web container via Solid Queue (Puma plugin). There is no separate jobs host and no database container.
+
+Open `https://<host>` and sign up with an email address. The code arrives through the mail server you configured.
+
+Later deploys:
+
+```sh
+kamal deploy
+```
+
+A console on the box: `kamal console`. Logs: `kamal logs`.
+
+### What persists
+
+The named volume `fizzy_storage` holds:
+
+- `production.sqlite3` and the queue, cache, and cable databases
+- Active Storage files (`storage/production/files`)
+
+Replacing the container does not replace the volume. Back it up out of band if the box matters. Changing the volume name or the `/rails/storage` path starts a fresh database.
